.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt ALSA-UTILS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm alsa-utils
.Nd ALSA playback, recording, mixer and MIDI tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm aplay
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl D Ar pcm
.Ar file
.Nm arecord
.Op Fl D Ar pcm
.Op Fl f Ar format
.Op Fl r Ar rate
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The GNU root includes Debian's alsa-utils package.
.Xr desktop 7
configures the default PCM as ALSA's plug converter over the OSS plugin.
.Nm aplay
plays a WAVE file through that PCM.
.Nm arecord
records from it.
.Fl D
selects another PCM; each program's
.Fl Fl help
lists its format and device options.
.Pp
.Nm speaker-test
plays generated tones.
.Nm alsabat
checks playback and capture, and
.Nm alsaloop
copies between capture and playback PCMs.
.Nm alsamixer
and
.Nm amixer
control ALSA mixers.
.Nm iecset
sets digital audio status.
.Nm alsactl
saves, restores and initializes ALSA card state.
.Nm alsa-info
collects diagnostic information, and
.Nm alsabat-test
runs the audio test script.
.Pp
.Nm aconnect
connects ALSA sequencer ports;
.Nm aplaymidi ,
.Nm aplaymidi2 ,
.Nm arecordmidi
and
.Nm arecordmidi2
play or record MIDI;
.Nm aseqdump
reads sequencer events,
.Nm aseqnet
relays them over the network, and
.Nm aseqsend
sends them.
.Nm amidi
reads or writes raw MIDI bytes.
.Nm axfer
transfers PCM frames.
.Nm alsatplg
compiles topology files,
.Nm alsaucm
manages use-case configuration, and
.Nm nhlt-dmic-info
reads digital microphone topology information.
.Sh LIMITS
Rach2 supplies OSS devices, without native ALSA card, sequencer or MIDI
kernel interfaces.
Tools that require those interfaces report no such device.
The default PCM's OSS route supports playback and capture as described in
.Xr dsp 4 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dsp 4 ,
.Xr desktop 7
